{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Phase 2 RED oracle and contract card. authoritative_contract: raw batched resolver may fail closed to {} (src/rebar/attest/authorship.py:294-378), while fixture equivalence must remain deterministic across documented transient Git reads (tests/_git_counts.py:1-55). trigger_preconditions: the first real broad git-log boundary returns rc128/empty, rc0/empty, or raises EAGAIN; the identical second attempt runs normally against the unchanged real fixture repo. production_path: test-local fixture resolver -> real build_ticket_position_commit_map -> real temp Git history. tier: real temporary repository with fault injection only at the subprocess return boundary; a pure mock would not prove the real parser/topology succeeds on replay. observable_postcondition: all 8 exact position->SHA pairs equal the per-event resolver, with exactly two broad attempts. negative_control: a persistent empty result stops after exactly five attempts and raises diagnostics containing fsck and count-objects output. collateral_invariants: production authorship source and fallback semantics remain unchanged. gate: make test.\n\nFinal oracle was observed legitimately RED before the fix: rc128, empty-success, and EAGAIN cases each failed because broad_calls was 1 rather than 2; the persistent case failed because no AssertionError was raised. pytest collected and executed all four cases (4 failed, 8 deselected in 1.96s). The behavioral failures are the missing bounded recovery/diagnostic behavior, not import or fixture errors."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786905457916404001,"uuid":"2d98a3e3-b9dd-40f9-8671-39b0c9767b6b"}